@page "/about"
@using OcadViewer.Wasm.Services
@inject Localiser L

@*
    Uses the Angular translations where keys exist. The sections below have no key
    because the Angular About page never said these things - they are about how
    this app renders maps, which is new. They stay English until someone who
    speaks Norwegian writes the translations; inventing them here would put bad
    Norwegian into a file the Angular app also reads.

    Also the home of the third-party notices, which the BSD-3 licence on the
    vendored renderer requires to travel with what is served to a browser.
*@

<PageTitle>@L["#_about"] @L["#_OCADVersioner"]</PageTitle>

<h1>@L["#_OCADVersioner"]</h1>

<p class="lead">@L["#_jumbo1Title"]</p>

<p>@L["#_projectDirectorySelectorText"]</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">How the map is drawn</h2>
<p>
    Maps are parsed and rendered by Purple Pen's map engine, compiled to
    WebAssembly and running entirely in your browser. Nothing is uploaded: the
    files stay on your machine and there is no server.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Credits and licences</h2>
<p>
    The OCAD parser and renderer come from
    <a href="https://github.com/petergolde/PurplePen" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Purple Pen</a>
    by Peter Golde, used under the BSD 3-Clause licence. The map viewport is
    Leaflet. Full notices for every third-party component are in
    <a href="third-party-notices.txt" target="_blank">third-party notices</a>.
</p>

<p class="text-muted small">
    This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Purple Pen or Peter Golde.
</p>
